    "title": "Bethea leads Delaware State in season-opening basketball loss to Temple - NewsBreak",
    "text": "7 hours ago\nPHILADELPHIA, Pa. — Zion Bethea netted a team-high 20 points but Delaware State fell to Temple, 83-65, in its men’s basketball season opener at the Liacouras Center on Wednesday night.\nThe Hornets never led in the contest but only trailed 35-27 at halftime.\nPonce James added 16 points for DelState with Ademar Santos coming off the bench to score 15.\nTemple sophomore Aiden Tobiason, the St. Elizabeth High grad, scored 16 of his game-high 23 points in the second half.\nA 6-foot-4 guard, Bethea is a transfer from Pepperdine playing for his fifth college program. Two years ago, he was at Delaware but played in only three games because of injuries.\nBethea has also been at St. Francis Brooklyn and Hofstra.\nDelState had 16 turnovers in the game and hit 24-of-54 shots from the floor for 44 percent. The Hornets sank 7-of-16 three-pointers with Bethea going 4-for-7 and Santos shooting 3-of-4 from beyond the arc.\nDelState is now 0-4 all-time against Temple with all four games played in Philadelphia.\nThe Hornets next play on Saturday at Syracuse as they start the season with four straight road games.",
